  "method": {
    "recorded": "Counted at generation time: the length of each generate() call's new tokens, which includes the end-of-sequence token, summed over every decision.",
    "rebuilt_from_logs": "Reconstructed after the fact, not counted at generation time. Each decoded completion in the episode log is re-tokenized with the model's pinned tokenizer, add_special_tokens=False, and counted as min(tokens + 1, max_new_tokens): decoding drops the end-of-sequence token, and a reply that hit the limit has none. At R1 the retry completion counts as its own decision.",
    "validation": "Before anything is written, the rule is applied to every Qwen3-1.7B run that recorded its counts and has its episode log, and must give back each recorded rung total exactly. The rule is not applied to Llama-3.1-8B; rule_on_llama shows what it gives there, beside the recorded totals that are kept.",
    "tokens_per_attempt": "tokens_total divided by episodes; one episode is one attempt.",
    "cost": "tokens_per_attempt times the model's unique parameters in billions (rounded)."
  },
  "max_new_tokens": 256,
  "parameters": {
    "convention": "Each parameter is counted once. A model whose config ties the output head to the embedding holds one matrix for both, so a stored copy of the head is not counted again. stored counts every tensor in the safetensors files; unique drops that copy. rounded_billions is the constant cost uses.",
